{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>ונשאתם את סכות</b> — from the root סכת, like הסכת ושמע. Its meaning is willing endurance, as also in the language of Ishmael: a person says to his fellow, סבתל״י, which means: bear my words and accept willingly." "And the word כיון is known in the language of Ishmael, for it is כיוא״ן. And the meaning of שבתי is that they made it an idol: <b>אשר עשיתם</b> — שב אל צלמיכם." "<b>וכוכב</b> — construct: the star of your Elohim. <b>עשיתם</b> — you made its image to worship it."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "The text of comment 1 is compressed and elliptical; rendered hyper-literally without smoothing. The relationship between כיון, כיוא״ן, and the surrounding argument is left as opaque as the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:15.541077219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}